# Upstream repositories, if any are cloned again for local study. During
# development these were read to understand how other tools behave. Sage and
# mzSniffer also supplied ported code, credited in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md;
# the others informed method only. The clones were removed at production
# time. See _dev/NOTES.md "Vendored upstream clones".
reference/

# Keep reference-notes/ (our distilled documentation)
#
# ANCHORED, and it must stay anchored. A bare `testing/` matches at EVERY level,
# so it swallowed `_dev/testing/` and silently refused new files there, including
# the `results.json` exception below. Git cannot re-include a file inside an
# excluded directory, so that exception simply stopped working and said nothing.
# The repository has no `testing/` at the root any more; it moved into `_dev/`.
/testing/

# Large test data files (mzML, FASTA, etc.)
*.mzML
*.mzML.gz
*.raw
*.RAW
*.fasta
*.FASTA
*.mgf
*.MGF

# Claude Code machine-local settings (permission grants, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Sage output files and directories (regenerated on each run)
*.sage.tsv
lfq.tsv
results.json
# ...EXCEPT under recon-output. Sage's own results.json is the ONLY honest record
# of what was searched: effective-params.json copies the TEMPLATE's database.fasta
# and Sage overrides it with the -f flag, so the tracked file could name a
# database that was never used. It did exactly that, and misled a session on
# 2026-09-01. The truth must be in git.
!/_dev/testing/recon-output/**/results.json
# Scratch verification runs. Never committed: recon has one artifact set
# (full-run/), and a second copy of a run is exactly the kind of stale ghost
# this repo has been cleaning out.
_dev/testing/recon-output/_verify/
_dev/testing/recon-output/_staging/
_dev/testing/recon-output/_regen/
_dev/testing/search-output/
_dev/testing/inputs/results.sage.tsv
_dev/testing/inputs/lfq.tsv

# Rust build artifacts (when we start building)
target/
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, on Ben's call 2026-09-02. recon is a binary crate,
# so the lockfile is the only thing that pins the dependency GRAPH. The Sage git
# rev pins Sage's SOURCE alone. Without this file every CI build re-resolved 335
# packages. Do not re-ignore it.

# IDE
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# MetaMorpheus raw and heavy outputs
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task1-CalibrateTask/*.mzML
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task1-CalibrateTask/*.mzID

_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task2-GPTMDTask/*.xml

_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*.mzML
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*.mzID
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*PSMs*.psmtsv
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*Peptides*.psmtsv
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*ProteinGroups*.tsv
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*Quantified*.tsv
_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/*FormattedForPercolator.tab

_dev/testing/reference-data/metamorpheus/*/Task3-SearchTask/Individual File Results/

# Generated by report_layout_mockup.py; the SCRIPT is the artefact, not its output.
_dev/testing/scripts/report_layout_mockup.html

# Captured build/test output. Regenerated on every run; the current numbers
# live in PLAN and NOTES. Two stale copies from 2026-08-24 were tracked until
# 2026-09-02.
*.log
